        "id": "q06",
        "answer": "KLK identifies physical and transition risks that could influence operations, supply chain, and financial performance [S1]. Specific principal risks reviewed by the Board include evolving regulatory and market landscapes [S2] and human rights violations in operations and supply chains [S2]. Sustainability and climate-related risks are categorized as principal risks for the financial year 2025 [S4].\n\nGovernance of these risks involves:\n*   The Board of Directors oversees sustainability and climate-related strategy, ensuring integration into long-term planning [S3].\n*   The Audit and Risk Committee oversees sustainability and climate-related matters with neutrality and independence [S3].\n*   The Group\u2019s approach is integrated into its three-lines-of-defence enterprise risk management model [S5].\n*   Operational management owns and manages risks day-to-day across four pillars of the sustainability framework (Marketplace, Environment, Workplace, Community) [S5].",
